WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.154
[Intro music]

00:00:06.954 --> 00:00:08.669
Good morning Hank, it's Thursday.

00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:11.010
Hank, I can't talk to you with both 
my mouth and my hair,

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.975
so I'm gonna talk to you with my hair.

00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:16.040
Hank, as you can no doubt see,
the puff continues to grow.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.880
Hank, I'd like to thank the yeti
for her endearing support of my hair,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.680
although I have to tell ya',

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.860
I think I'm beginning to lose the will.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.439
Enjoy the puff now, 
because the next time I see you

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:26.869
I think it's gonna be gone.

00:00:26.969 --> 00:00:27.475
In other news,

00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:30.180
Hank, I really wanna do 
a Question Tuesday on Tuesday,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.089
but I don't really have anything else 
I wanna talk about today,

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:35.960
so instead I'm going to include some outtakes
from last week's Question Tuesday.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.040
Nerdfighters, in the next Question Tuesday

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.530
I'm going to try to break the world record for 
most questions answered in a four-minute period

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:42.580
but I need your help.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.510
Leave your questions in the comments,
and if I don't answer them all in the video

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.170
I'll try to answer them in a gigantic blog
post at the ning.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:52.195
And now: the outtakes. 
Take it away, me-from-two-weeks-ago:

00:00:52.295 --> 00:00:56.120
"Corn dog meets mint chocolate chip ice cream
in a dark alley - who wins?"

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.230
Oh, I'll tell ya' who wins: everybody.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.080
You fry up a corn dog,
you stick it in some semi-melted

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.850
mint chocolate chip ice cream,
and you've got the greatest innovation

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.170
in deliciousness 
since  the deep-fried twinkie.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.740
"What's your favorite graphic novel 
of all time?"

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.170
There's a lot of great ones, but I'm gonna
go with Maus by Art Spiegelman.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.220
"If you were going on a long trip 
to the evil baby orphanage

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.600
and could only take two CD's with you, 
which would they be?"

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.870
A Love Supreme by John Coltrane 
and something by the Mountain Goats.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.160
Although honestly, it wouldn't matter, 
since evil baby Stalin

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.930
is probably just gonna steal my CD's.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.300
"You get to have a one-hour conversation 
with a Disney character.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.509
Who would it be?"

00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:26.440
Probably Mickey; I'd like to ask him 
how it feels

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.520
to be single-handedly responsible 
for the death

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.480
of reasonable American copyright law.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.540
"What's the most interesting 
nickname you've ever had?"

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.279
One time in high school

00:01:33.379 --> 00:01:36.419
I made the mistake of saying that 
Christian Slater had never made a bad movie,

00:01:36.519 --> 00:01:38.950
and for a long time after that 
people called me Kuffs.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.080
"Why do you think that all the most viewed
vlogbrothers videos are by Hank?"

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.890
I don't know.
Probably because he's funnier?

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:46.460
Although, in one case, 
it seems to be almost entirely

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.799
because the screen shot 
is of two giraffes having sex.

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:52.200
I don't know what that says 
about the Youtube community.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.665
I guess it just says that 

00:01:53.765 --> 00:01:56.930
"We're people who love giraffes 
who love girrafes."

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.500
"If you had to pick one pattern
to have all your clothes made out of,

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.430
what would it be?"

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:01.860
Definitely argyle.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.129
Honestly, I don't even understand the point
of wearing socks unless they're argyles.

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:07.509
"What's the most embarrassing song 
you know all the lyrics to?"

00:02:07.609 --> 00:02:08.800
[Speaking poetically] 
When I'm not with you,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.990
I lose my mind.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.905
Just give me a sign.

00:02:12.005 --> 00:02:14.619
Hit me, baby, one more time.

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:16.789
"If you had to vote for a republican 
presidential candidate,

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:17.459
who would it be?"

00:02:17.559 --> 00:02:19.029
Definitely Abraham Lincoln.

00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:22.029
Oh wait, do you mean like a 
living republican presidential candidate?

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:24.689
Well, first-off, I don't vote for the party,
I vote for the individual.

00:02:24.789 --> 00:02:27.349
And second-off, I don't want to vote for 
any of those guys.

00:02:27.449 --> 00:02:30.080
"Why wouldn't you let Maureen Johnson,
who had read your new book Paper Towns,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.500
talk about Paper Towns?"

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.620
The same reason I won't let 
Hank talk about Paper Towns:

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.359
It's secret.

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:38.719
"A plane crashed, and every 
single person on board was killed,

00:02:38.819 --> 00:02:41.240
but there were still survivors. 
How is that possible?"

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.180
Every single person on board was killed,
but many married people survived.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.955
Just one of the many benefits.

00:02:47.055 --> 00:02:48.829
Oh hey, Riddle, I've got one for you:

00:02:48.929 --> 00:02:52.010
What's the only word in the 
English language that starts with 'PW'?

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.515
"The Iliad or the Odyssey?"

00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:54.219
The Odyssey.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:55.975
"Has Helen Hunt seen The Helen Hunt Song yet?"

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.130
No; keep fighting!

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.180
"How old is the yeti?"

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:58.730
Twenty-eight.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.350
"Will we ever get to see the yeti?"

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.969
I don't know; maybe, if you have a lot of money

00:03:02.069 --> 00:03:04.560
and can afford to go on long expeditions to Nepal.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.309
"Which one of the presidential candidates

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:07.675
would you most wanna play Twister with?"

00:03:07.775 --> 00:03:08.940
Hmm, that's tough.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.089
I guess Mike Huckabee because, you know,
he doesn't look very flexible, and so I think

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:13.585
I'd have an advantage.

00:03:13.685 --> 00:03:14.880
I would wanna play Twister with Ron Paul,

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.359
but the problem with that is that 
Ron Paul's version of Twister

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:19.989
only has yellow dots 
because Ron Paul felt that it would

00:03:20.089 --> 00:03:23.819
offer more freedom of choice and also be 
less expensive if the game eliminated

00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:25.789
the red dots,
the blue dots, and the green dots.

00:03:25.889 --> 00:03:26.954
And also the spinner.

00:03:27.054 --> 00:03:29.519
And now, Hank, I will be attacked 
by Ron Paul's minions.

00:03:29.619 --> 00:03:31.969
Don't hate me guys, it was just a Twister joke.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:34.939
Nerdfighters, as always, thanks for your questions.

00:03:35.039 --> 00:03:37.539
Pufflevels? ...I'm gonna miss ya, buddy.

